#. type: Title ==
#: src/en/01-scope.adoc:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "Scope"
msgstr "Alcance"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/01-scope.adoc:5
msgid ""
"This standard specifies requirements for protecting <<term-member-data,member"
" data>> throughout its life cycle. It applies to every <<term-entity,entity>>"
" that stores, processes or transmits member data, and to every <<term-system-"
"component,system component>> included in, or connected to, the <<term-member-"
"data-environment,member data environment>>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/01-scope.adoc:7
msgid ""
"This standard does not specify how an entity organises its staff, and it does"
" not replace legal or contractual obligations that apply to the entity."
msgstr ""
"Esta norma no especifica cómo organiza una entidad a su personal, ni "
"sustituye a las obligaciones legales o contractuales aplicables a la entidad."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/01-scope.adoc:9
msgid "Each requirement in clauses 4 to 6 consists of four parts:"
msgstr "Cada requisito de los capítulos 4 a 6 consta de cuatro partes:"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/01-scope.adoc:11
msgid "a stable identifier, which matches the clause number;"
msgstr "un identificador estable, que coincide con el número del apartado;"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/01-scope.adoc:12
msgid "the requirement statement, which is normative;"
msgstr "el enunciado del requisito, que es normativo;"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/01-scope.adoc:13
msgid ""
"one or more testing procedures, which an <<term-assessor,assessor>> follows "
"to confirm that the requirement is met;"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/01-scope.adoc:14
msgid "guidance, which is informative."
msgstr "orientación, que es informativa."

#. type: Title ===
#: src/en/01-scope.adoc:16
#, no-wrap
msgid "Requirement language"
msgstr "Lenguaje de los requisitos"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/01-scope.adoc:18
msgid ""
"In this standard the word \"shall\" indicates a requirement, the word "
"\"should\" indicates a recommendation, and the word \"may\" indicates a "
"permission. These words carry that meaning only in normative clauses. "
"Guidance, notes, the annex and the bibliography are informative."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: src/en/02-normative-references.adoc:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "Normative references"
msgstr "Referencias normativas"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/02-normative-references.adoc:5
msgid ""
"The following documents are referred to in the text in such a way that some "
"or all of their content constitutes requirements of this standard."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/02-normative-references.adoc:7
msgid ""
"[[ref-rfc8446]]IETF RFC 8446, _The Transport Layer Security (TLS) Protocol "
"Version 1.3_. Available at https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/02-normative-references.adoc:7
msgid ""
"[[ref-rfc3339]]IETF RFC 3339, _Date and Time on the Internet: Timestamps_. "
"Available at https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc3339."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: src/en/03-terms.adoc:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "Terms and definitions"
msgstr "Términos y definiciones"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/03-terms.adoc:5
msgid ""
"For the purposes of this standard, the following terms and definitions apply."
msgstr ""
"A efectos de esta norma, se aplican los términos y definiciones siguientes."

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/en/03-terms.adoc:6
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[term-assessor]]assessor"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/03-terms.adoc:8
msgid ""
"person or organisation that evaluates whether an entity meets the "
"requirements of this standard"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/en/03-terms.adoc:9
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[term-entity]]entity"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/03-terms.adoc:11
msgid "organisation that stores, processes or transmits member data"
msgstr "organización que almacena, procesa o transmite datos de miembros"

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/en/03-terms.adoc:12
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[term-member-data]]member data"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/03-terms.adoc:14
msgid ""
"information that identifies a member, together with any account or "
"transaction information linked to that member"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/en/03-terms.adoc:15
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[term-member-data-environment]]member data environment"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/03-terms.adoc:17
msgid ""
"people, processes and system components that store, process or transmit "
"member data"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/en/03-terms.adoc:18
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[term-privileged-account]]privileged account"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/03-terms.adoc:20
msgid ""
"account with permissions beyond those of a standard user, such as the ability"
" to change security settings or read all member data"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/en/03-terms.adoc:21
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[term-strong-cryptography]]strong cryptography"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/03-terms.adoc:23
msgid ""
"cryptography based on publicly reviewed algorithms with an effective key "
"strength of at least 128 bits"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/en/03-terms.adoc:24
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[term-system-component]]system component"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/03-terms.adoc:26
msgid ""
"network device, server, computing device, virtual component or application "
"included in or connected to the member data environment"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/en/03-terms.adoc:27
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[term-user-identifier]]user identifier"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/03-terms.adoc:28
msgid ""
"value that uniquely identifies one person or one automated process to a "
"system component"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: src/en/04-access-management.adoc:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "Access management"
msgstr "Gestión de accesos"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/04-access-management.adoc:5
msgid ""
"Access to member data is limited to people and processes that need it, and "
"every action can be traced to the person or process that performed it."
msgstr ""
"El acceso a los datos de miembros se limita a las personas y procesos que lo "
"necesitan, y toda acción puede atribuirse a la persona o proceso que la "
"realizó."

#. type: Title ===
#: src/en/04-access-management.adoc:7
#, no-wrap
msgid "Identification"
msgstr "Identificación"

#. type: Table
#: src/en/04-access-management.adoc:11 src/en/annex-a-guidance.adoc:27
#, no-wrap
msgid "Unique user identifiers"
msgstr "Identificadores de usuario únicos"

#. type: .statement
#: src/en/04-access-management.adoc:16
msgid ""
"The entity shall assign a unique <<term-user-identifier,user identifier>> to "
"each person and each automated process before allowing access to any <<term-"
"system-component,system component>>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: src/en/04-access-management.adoc:19 src/en/04-access-management.adoc:39
#: src/en/04-access-management.adoc:64 src/en/05-data-protection.adoc:21
#: src/en/05-data-protection.adoc:41 src/en/05-data-protection.adoc:66
#: src/en/06-logging-monitoring.adoc:24 src/en/06-logging-monitoring.adoc:44
#, no-wrap
msgid "Testing procedures"
msgstr "Procedimientos de prueba"

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/en/04-access-management.adoc:20
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[TP-4.1.1.a]]4.1.1.a"
msgstr ""

#. type: .testing
#: src/en/04-access-management.adoc:21
msgid ""
"Examine the account management procedure to verify that it requires a unique "
"user identifier for each person and each automated process."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/en/04-access-management.adoc:21
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[TP-4.1.1.b]]4.1.1.b"
msgstr ""

#. type: .testing
#: src/en/04-access-management.adoc:22
msgid ""
"Examine the account list of a sample of system components to verify that no "
"user identifier is assigned to more than one person."
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: src/en/04-access-management.adoc:24 src/en/04-access-management.adoc:44
#: src/en/04-access-management.adoc:70 src/en/05-data-protection.adoc:26
#: src/en/05-data-protection.adoc:46 src/en/05-data-protection.adoc:71
#: src/en/06-logging-monitoring.adoc:29 src/en/06-logging-monitoring.adoc:50
#, no-wrap
msgid "Guidance"
msgstr "Orientación"

#. type: delimited block *
#: src/en/04-access-management.adoc:27
msgid ""
"When several people share one identifier, actions cannot be traced to an "
"individual. Service accounts used by software are in scope: each one needs "
"its own identifier and a named owner."
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: src/en/04-access-management.adoc:31 src/en/annex-a-guidance.adoc:28
#, no-wrap
msgid "Removal of access on departure"
msgstr "Retirada del acceso al cesar la relación"

#. type: .statement
#: src/en/04-access-management.adoc:36
msgid ""
"The entity shall disable the user identifiers of a person within one business"
" day of that person leaving the entity."
msgstr ""
"La entidad debe deshabilitar los identificadores de usuario de una persona en"
" el plazo de un día hábil desde que dicha persona abandone la entidad."

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/en/04-access-management.adoc:40
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[TP-4.1.2.a]]4.1.2.a"
msgstr ""

#. type: .testing
#: src/en/04-access-management.adoc:41
msgid ""
"Examine the leaver procedure to verify that it defines who disables user "
"identifiers and within what time."
msgstr ""
"Examinar el procedimiento de bajas para verificar que define quién "
"deshabilita los identificadores de usuario y en qué plazo."

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/en/04-access-management.adoc:41
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[TP-4.1.2.b]]4.1.2.b"
msgstr ""

#. type: .testing
#: src/en/04-access-management.adoc:42
msgid ""
"Examine records for a sample of people who left in the last six months to "
"verify that their user identifiers were disabled within one business day."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block *
#: src/en/04-access-management.adoc:47
msgid ""
"Accounts that remain active after a person leaves are a common route for "
"unauthorised access. Linking the leaver procedure to the human resources "
"system reduces the delay."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/en/04-access-management.adoc:50
#, no-wrap
msgid "Access review"
msgstr "Revisión de accesos"

#. type: Table
#: src/en/04-access-management.adoc:54 src/en/annex-a-guidance.adoc:29
#, no-wrap
msgid "Periodic review of access rights"
msgstr "Revisión periódica de los derechos de acceso"

#. type: .statement
#: src/en/04-access-management.adoc:59
msgid ""
"The entity shall review access rights at least as often as <<table-review-"
"frequency>> specifies, and shall remove any access that is no longer needed."
msgstr ""

#. type: .statement
#: src/en/04-access-management.adoc:61
msgid ""
"The entity should record the outcome of each review, including the name of "
"the reviewer."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/en/04-access-management.adoc:65
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[TP-4.2.1.a]]4.2.1.a"
msgstr ""

#. type: .testing
#: src/en/04-access-management.adoc:66
msgid ""
"Examine review records to verify that reviews took place at the frequency "
"that <<table-review-frequency>> specifies."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/en/04-access-management.adoc:66
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[TP-4.2.1.b]]4.2.1.b"
msgstr ""

#. type: .testing
#: src/en/04-access-management.adoc:67
msgid ""
"Interview the people responsible to verify that access identified as no "
"longer needed was removed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/en/04-access-management.adoc:67
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[TP-4.2.1.c]]4.2.1.c"
msgstr ""

#. type: .testing
#: src/en/04-access-management.adoc:68
msgid ""
"Examine a sample of <<term-privileged-account,privileged accounts>> to verify"
" that each one has a documented business reason."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block *
#: src/en/04-access-management.adoc:73
msgid ""
"Access tends to accumulate as people change roles. A review is most effective"
" when the person who performs it understands what each role needs."
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: src/en/04-access-management.adoc:76
#, no-wrap
msgid "Minimum frequency of access reviews"
msgstr "Frecuencia mínima de las revisiones de acceso"

#. type: Table
#: src/en/04-access-management.adoc:79
#, no-wrap
msgid "Account type"
msgstr "Tipo de cuenta"

#. type: Table
#: src/en/04-access-management.adoc:79
#, no-wrap
msgid "Minimum review frequency"
msgstr "Frecuencia mínima de revisión"

#. type: Table
#: src/en/04-access-management.adoc:81
#, no-wrap
msgid "Reviewer"
msgstr "Revisor"

#. type: Table
#: src/en/04-access-management.adoc:82
#, no-wrap
msgid "Standard user account"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: src/en/04-access-management.adoc:83
#, no-wrap
msgid "Every 12 months"
msgstr "Cada 12 meses"

#. type: Table
#: src/en/04-access-management.adoc:85
#, no-wrap
msgid "Line manager of the account holder"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: src/en/04-access-management.adoc:86
#, no-wrap
msgid "<<term-privileged-account,Privileged account>>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: src/en/04-access-management.adoc:87
#, no-wrap
msgid "Every 3 months"
msgstr "Cada 3 meses"

#. type: Table
#: src/en/04-access-management.adoc:89
#, no-wrap
msgid "System owner"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: src/en/04-access-management.adoc:90
#, no-wrap
msgid "After any change of role"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: src/en/04-access-management.adoc:92
#, no-wrap
msgid "System owner and security function"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: src/en/04-access-management.adoc:93
#, no-wrap
msgid "Account used by an automated process"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: src/en/04-access-management.adoc:94
#, no-wrap
msgid "Every 6 months"
msgstr "Cada 6 meses"

#. type: Table
#: src/en/04-access-management.adoc:95
#, no-wrap
msgid "Named owner of the process"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: src/en/05-data-protection.adoc:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "Data protection"
msgstr "Protección de datos"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/05-data-protection.adoc:5
msgid ""
"Member data is unreadable to anyone who obtains it without authorisation, "
"whether it is stored or in transit."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/en/05-data-protection.adoc:7
#, no-wrap
msgid "Storage"
msgstr "Almacenamiento"

#. type: Table
#: src/en/05-data-protection.adoc:11 src/en/annex-a-guidance.adoc:30
#, no-wrap
msgid "Encryption of stored member data"
msgstr ""

#. type: .statement
#: src/en/05-data-protection.adoc:16
msgid ""
"The entity shall render stored <<term-member-data,member data>> unreadable by"
" using <<term-strong-cryptography,strong cryptography>>."
msgstr ""

#. type: .statement
#: src/en/05-data-protection.adoc:18
msgid ""
"The entity shall store cryptographic keys separately from the data that they "
"protect."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/en/05-data-protection.adoc:22
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[TP-5.1.1.a]]5.1.1.a"
msgstr ""

#. type: .testing
#: src/en/05-data-protection.adoc:23
msgid ""
"Examine system configurations to verify that stored member data is encrypted "
"with strong cryptography."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/en/05-data-protection.adoc:23
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[TP-5.1.1.b]]5.1.1.b"
msgstr ""

#. type: .testing
#: src/en/05-data-protection.adoc:24
msgid ""
"Examine key storage locations to verify that keys are not stored with the "
"data that they protect."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block *
#: src/en/05-data-protection.adoc:29
msgid ""
"Encryption protects data only while the keys stay secret. A key stored beside"
" the data that it protects gives little protection if the storage is "
"copied.footnote:[Hardware security modules and managed key services are two "
"common ways to separate keys from data.]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: src/en/05-data-protection.adoc:33 src/en/annex-a-guidance.adoc:31
#, no-wrap
msgid "Retention limits"
msgstr ""

#. type: .statement
#: src/en/05-data-protection.adoc:38
msgid ""
"The entity shall define a retention period for each category of member data, "
"and shall securely delete member data when its retention period ends."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/en/05-data-protection.adoc:42
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[TP-5.1.2.a]]5.1.2.a"
msgstr ""

#. type: .testing
#: src/en/05-data-protection.adoc:43
msgid ""
"Examine the retention policy to verify that it defines a retention period for"
" each category of member data."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/en/05-data-protection.adoc:43
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[TP-5.1.2.b]]5.1.2.b"
msgstr ""

#. type: .testing
#: src/en/05-data-protection.adoc:44
msgid ""
"Examine a sample of data stores to verify that they hold no member data older"
" than the defined retention period."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block *
#: src/en/05-data-protection.adoc:49
msgid ""
"Data that has been deleted cannot be stolen. Automated deletion jobs are more"
" reliable than manual clean-up."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/en/05-data-protection.adoc:52
#, no-wrap
msgid "Transmission"
msgstr "Transmisión"

#. type: Table
#: src/en/05-data-protection.adoc:56 src/en/annex-a-guidance.adoc:32
#, no-wrap
msgid "Encryption in transit"
msgstr ""

#. type: .statement
#: src/en/05-data-protection.adoc:61
msgid ""
"The entity shall protect member data sent over any network outside its "
"control by using Transport Layer Security version 1.3, as specified in <<ref-"
"rfc8446,IETF RFC 8446>>, or a protocol of equivalent strength."
msgstr ""

#. type: .statement
#: src/en/05-data-protection.adoc:63
msgid ""
"The entity may use an earlier protocol version on an internal network segment"
" that carries no member data."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/en/05-data-protection.adoc:67
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[TP-5.2.1.a]]5.2.1.a"
msgstr ""

#. type: .testing
#: src/en/05-data-protection.adoc:68
msgid ""
"Examine the configuration of a sample of external connections to verify that "
"they accept only the protocol versions that the requirement allows."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/en/05-data-protection.adoc:68
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[TP-5.2.1.b]]5.2.1.b"
msgstr ""

#. type: .testing
#: src/en/05-data-protection.adoc:69
msgid ""
"Observe a sample of transmissions to verify that member data is encrypted in "
"transit."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block *
#: src/en/05-data-protection.adoc:74
msgid ""
"Networks outside the control of the entity include the internet, wireless "
"networks and links operated by third parties. <<figure-data-flow>> shows "
"where encryption applies."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: src/en/06-logging-monitoring.adoc:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "Logging and monitoring"
msgstr "Registro y supervisión"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/06-logging-monitoring.adoc:5
msgid ""
"Activity that affects member data is recorded, kept and reviewed so that "
"misuse can be detected and investigated."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/en/06-logging-monitoring.adoc:7
#, no-wrap
msgid "Audit logs"
msgstr "Registros de auditoría"

#. type: Table
#: src/en/06-logging-monitoring.adoc:11 src/en/annex-a-guidance.adoc:33
#, no-wrap
msgid "Recording of access to member data"
msgstr ""

#. type: .statement
#: src/en/06-logging-monitoring.adoc:16
msgid ""
"The entity shall record every access to member data in an audit log. Each log"
" entry shall include:"
msgstr ""

#. type: .statement
#: src/en/06-logging-monitoring.adoc:18
msgid "the <<term-user-identifier,user identifier>>;"
msgstr ""

#. type: .statement
#: src/en/06-logging-monitoring.adoc:19
msgid ""
"the date and time, in the format that <<ref-rfc3339,IETF RFC 3339>> "
"specifies;"
msgstr ""

#. type: .statement
#: src/en/06-logging-monitoring.adoc:20
msgid "the action performed;"
msgstr ""

#. type: .statement
#: src/en/06-logging-monitoring.adoc:21
msgid "whether the action succeeded."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/en/06-logging-monitoring.adoc:25
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[TP-6.1.1.a]]6.1.1.a"
msgstr ""

#. type: .testing
#: src/en/06-logging-monitoring.adoc:26
msgid ""
"Examine logging configurations to verify that access to member data is "
"recorded."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/en/06-logging-monitoring.adoc:26
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[TP-6.1.1.b]]6.1.1.b"
msgstr ""

#. type: .testing
#: src/en/06-logging-monitoring.adoc:27
msgid ""
"Examine a sample of log entries to verify that each one includes all the "
"listed fields."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block *
#: src/en/06-logging-monitoring.adoc:32
msgid ""
"A log that omits the user identifier cannot support an investigation. A "
"single time format across all system components makes it possible to place "
"events in order."
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: src/en/06-logging-monitoring.adoc:36 src/en/annex-a-guidance.adoc:34
#, no-wrap
msgid "Retention and review of audit logs"
msgstr ""

#. type: .statement
#: src/en/06-logging-monitoring.adoc:41
msgid ""
"The entity shall keep audit logs for at least 12 months, and shall review "
"them for unusual activity at least once each week."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/en/06-logging-monitoring.adoc:45
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[TP-6.1.2.a]]6.1.2.a"
msgstr ""

#. type: .testing
#: src/en/06-logging-monitoring.adoc:46
msgid ""
"Examine log storage to verify that audit logs from the last 12 months are "
"available."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/en/06-logging-monitoring.adoc:46
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[TP-6.1.2.b]]6.1.2.b"
msgstr ""

#. type: .testing
#: src/en/06-logging-monitoring.adoc:47
msgid ""
"Examine review records to verify that reviews took place at least once each "
"week."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/en/06-logging-monitoring.adoc:47
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[TP-6.1.2.c]]6.1.2.c"
msgstr ""

#. type: .testing
#: src/en/06-logging-monitoring.adoc:48
msgid ""
"Interview the people responsible to verify that they follow up on unusual "
"activity."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block *
#: src/en/06-logging-monitoring.adoc:53
msgid ""
"Many incidents are discovered months after they begin. Automated alerting can"
" support the weekly review but does not replace it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: src/en/annex-a-guidance.adoc:3
#, no-wrap
msgid "Implementation guidance (informative)"
msgstr ""

#. type: appendix.informative
#: src/en/annex-a-guidance.adoc:6
msgid ""
"This annex gives additional information to help an entity apply the "
"requirements. It contains no requirements."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/en/annex-a-guidance.adoc:8
#, no-wrap
msgid "Where encryption applies"
msgstr ""

#. type: appendix.informative
#: src/en/annex-a-guidance.adoc:11
msgid ""
"<<figure-data-flow>> shows a typical flow of member data. Encryption in "
"transit, described in <<REQ-5.2.1>>, applies to the link between the member "
